<title>SINGAPORE: Inchcape sells JV insurance unit to Aon.</title>
<headline>Inchcape sells JV insurance unit to Aon.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inchcape Berhad said on Tuesday it had sold its stake in Inchcape Insurance Brokers Pte Ltd to Aon Holdings Asia B.V, the company's joint venture partner in the firm.</p>
<p>Aon Holdings Asia B.V. is a unit of U.S. broking giant Aon Corp.</p>
<p>The Singapore $2.17 million deal should realise a profit of about S$1.1 million for Inchcape, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>Inchcape said the sale was in line with its stated aim of exiting non-core businesses.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
